<title>BULGARIA: Yield down to 6.72 pct on Bulgaria 3-mth T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield down to 6.72 pct on Bulgaria 3-mth T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield to maturity on Bulgaria's Finance ministry three-month discount T-bills fell to 6.72 percent at Monday's auction from 10.13 percent a week earlier, central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with a par value of 10 billion levs and no minimum acceptable price set in advance and was fully sold.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		 BG3037797001</p>
<p> Maturity		     three months</p>
<p> Par value		    10,000 million levs</p>
<p> Auction date		 June 9</p>
<p> Issue date		   June 11</p>
<p> Maturity date		September 10</p>
<p> Bids received		70,868.7 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	  92.11 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		10,000 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	 93.70 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity    6.72 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
</text>
